+# What a System is
+
+A System is **more than a page — "a whole system of rules"** (the owner's own words,
+`public/framework/ai/2026-09-30/ui-system/requirements.md`, ask 1). Design is not just a url;
+it is layout, color, navigation, content and UI, all governed the same way, with its own
+action (the Inbox) and its own map of parts (the concept tiles). `System`
+(`core/System/System.js`) is the one class that carries that shape — Design, Code, UI and UX
+are all a `System` already. A change to the class reaches every one of them at once.
+
+## How to add one
+
+Two ways, both already written out in `System.js`'s own doc comment at the top of the file:
+
+1. **`page.js`** — construct it directly, like any other page:
+   ```js
+   export default new System({
+       meta: import.meta,
+       title: "Design", icon: "palette",
+       children: "layout color navigation content ui",
+       concepts: [{ name: "Layout", slug: "layout", icon: "view_quilt" }, …],
+       omit: "parts",
+       content(){ md("…"); },
+   });
+   ```
+2. **`page.jsonl`, with no `page.js` at all** — line 1 names the class, and `Log.js`'s
+   `log_class()` loads that module before constructing anything:
+   ```json
+   {"class": "/framework/core/System/System.js", "title": "Demo", "concepts": [...]}
+   ```
+
+Either way you get, for free: the Overview's concept tiles (`concepts:`), the readme folded
+in at the end of the Overview, an Inbox tab (turn it off with `inbox: false`), and `omit:` —
+one word to drop a derived tab or every declared child from the top strip without taking away
+its own url.
+
+## Open question
+
+Should `System` also replace the plain class-doc page for a core class that is really a
+system in its own right — `Page`, `View`, `App` — since a System's whole feature is top tabs,
+and a class-doc page's whole feature is the same top tabs? Not decided (the owner, 2026-10-01,
+`ui-system/requirements.md` ask 13) — recorded here rather than built, since this task's fence
+is `core/System/` only.
