--- /dev/null
+++ b/public/framework/core/System/readme.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# System — one shared page template behind Design, Code, UI, UX and (soon) AI
+
+`core/System/System.js` extends [Doc](/framework/ext/Doc/): the same top-tab strip
+(Overview · Inbox · its own parts · API · Docs · Files), the same concept tiles on the
+Overview, and the same Inbox tab, on every system page. Fix something here and all five
+improve for free. Full story: [the page](/framework/core/System/), [doc/system.md](./doc/system.md).
+
+## Use
+```js
+export default new System({
+    meta: import.meta,
+    title: "Design", icon: "palette",
+    children: "layout color navigation content ui",
+    concepts: [{ name: "Layout", slug: "layout", icon: "view_quilt" }, …],
+    omit: "parts",          // the parts are tiles on the Overview, not tabs
+    content(){ md("…"); },  // the intro, between the tiles and the readme
+});
+```
+Or, with no `page.js` at all, line 1 of a `page.jsonl`:
+```json
+{"class": "/framework/core/System/System.js", "title": "Demo", "concepts": [...]}
+```
+
+## The five systems
+- [Design](/framework/design/) — layout, color, navigation, content, UI
+- [Code](/framework/code/) — patterns, dos-and-don'ts, CSS, objects
+- [UI](/framework/ui/) — the component library
+- [UX](/framework/ux/) — the behavior classes
+- AI: pending — `/framework/ai/` is still a plain `Page`; converting it is the next step
+
+## Watch out
+- `omit:` is the one word that drops a tab — a derived one (`"api"`, `"overview"`, `"inbox"`,
+  `"doc"`, `"files"`) or every declared child at once (`"parts"`) — without hiding that
+  child's own url.
+- `ext("Inbox")` is idempotent on purpose: a `page.jsonl` line may ALSO carry
+  `{"ext": "Inbox"}`, and running setup() twice would empty `page.inbox` and double up every
+  later line.
+
+## More
+- [Overview](/framework/core/System/) · [`doc/system.md`](./doc/system.md) — what a System is
+  (more than a page) and the two ways to add one.
+- Files: `System.js` (the class) · `page.js` (System documenting System)
